  "_mentionsComment": [
    "Mention-grammar parity rows (`@chat:` / `@lane:` / `@term:`). `text` is a",
    "whole message body, not a bare token, because the grammar is boundary-",
    "sensitive: the desktop's regex only matches after start-of-string or one of",
    "[ \\t\\r\\n ( [ { , ], which is what keeps emails and `foo@chat:bar` out.",
    "",
    "`chips` lists every chip the unified one-pass parser must emit, in document",
    "order, with no overlaps — mentions AND links together. An empty list means",
    "the text must produce no chips at all."
  ],
